PART 1: XYZ SPATIAL-TEMPORAL FOUNDATION
Design the experience across three axes:
X-Axis: Distance (Reach & Scale)
	•	X1 — Personal (1-10): Intimate gatherings, private experiences
	•	X2 — Local (10-100): Community events, pop-ups
	•	X3 — Regional (100-1,000): City-wide activations, festivals
	•	X4 — National (1,000-10,000): Multi-city tours, branded experiences
	•	X5 — Global (10,000+): Worldwide simultaneous events
Y-Axis: Space (Physical Footprint)
	•	Y1 — Contained (Single room/booth)
	•	Y2 — Venue (Single building)
	•	Y3 — Campus (Multiple buildings)
	•	Y4 — District (City section)
	•	Y5 — Boundless (City-wide/virtual)
Z-Axis: Time (Duration)
	•	Z1 — Moment (< 1 hour)
	•	Z2 — Session (1-4 hours)
	•	Z3 — Day (4-12 hours)
	•	Z4 — Extended (Multi-day)
	•	Z5 — Persistent (Ongoing)

PART 2: 5 SENSES ACTIVATION MATRIX
For each sense, define specific activations tied to the creative concept:
SIGHT
Color palette, lighting design, scenic elements, projection/video, costume design, graphic design.
SOUND
Original score, sound effects, spatial audio, live music, ambient soundscapes, interactive triggers.
TOUCH
Texture palette, temperature, interactive elements, haptics, wearables, tactile wayfinding.
TASTE
Signature food/beverages, interactive dining, flavor progression, dietary accommodations.
SMELL
Signature scent, zone-specific scenting, scent triggers, aroma integration, scent-memory activation.

PART 3: URL→IRL LIFECYCLE
Phase 1: Digital Pre-Event (URL)
Discovery, engagement, transaction, anticipation, preparation.
Phase 2: Hybrid Threshold In
Arrival, transition, orientation, onboarding.
Phase 3: Physical Event (IRL)
Core experience, peak moments, interactive elements, social touchpoints, support services.
Phase 4: Hybrid Threshold Out
Resolution, transition, retail opportunity, documentation.
Phase 5: Digital Post-Event (URL)
Follow-up, content distribution, community continuation, re-engagement, advocacy activation.

