PART 6: DATABASE ARCHITECTURE (NEW v4.0)
Complete data-driven production management with API connectivity:
9.1 Schema Overview (45+ Tables)
	•	Core: organizations, productions, venues, zones
	•	People: contacts, departments, roles, production_assignments
	•	Credentials: credential_types, credentials, credential_zone_access
	•	Scheduling: schedule_phases, schedule_tasks, task_contingencies
	•	Shows: shows, cues
	•	Contracts: contract_types, contracts
	•	Compliance: permits, insurance_policies, compliance_checklists, compliance_items
	•	Sponsors/Investors: sponsor_tiers, sponsors, investors, investment_rounds, investments
	•	SOPs: sop_categories, sops, sop_steps
	•	Reporting: incidents, lost_found_items, expenses, expense_reports, daily_reports, wrap_reports
	•	API: api_keys, webhooks, integrations, sync_logs, audit_logs
	•	Metrics: metrics (normalized KPIs)
9.2 Design Principles
	•	Third Normal Form (3NF) — Eliminate redundancy
	•	UUID Primary Keys — Global uniqueness for API compatibility
	•	Soft Deletes — deleted_at timestamps for audit trails
	•	Comprehensive Audit — created_at, updated_at, created_by, updated_by
	•	Multi-Tenancy — organization_id on all tenant-scoped tables
	•	JSONB Metadata — Flexible extensibility fields
	•	Row Level Security — Supabase RLS for data isolation
9.3 API Integration
RESTful endpoints via Supabase: https://{project}.supabase.co/rest/v1/{table}
	•	Operations: GET (list/read), POST (create), PATCH (update), DELETE
	•	Query params: ?status=eq.active, ?select=id,title, ?order=created_at.desc
	•	Nested resources: ?select=*,venue:venues(name,address)
9.4 Integration Mappings
	•	Slack — Real-time notifications, task assignments, incident alerts
	•	Notion — Production databases synced as pages
	•	Airtable — Table-to-base mapping with field conversion
	•	Monday.com — Board sync with status/timeline mapping
	•	Asana — Project sync with task dependencies
	•	Google Workspace — Calendar, Drive, Sheets integration
	•	Microsoft 365 — Teams, SharePoint, Excel integration
	•	Zapier/Make — Webhook triggers for custom automation
9.5 Webhook Events
	•	production.created / .updated / .status_changed
	•	show.scheduled / .started / .completed
	•	incident.created / .escalated / .resolved
	•	task.created / .assigned / .status_changed / .overdue
	•	contract.created / .signed / .expiring
	•	sponsor.confirmed / .payment_received
	•	credential.issued / .revoked
	•	expense.submitted / .approved
9.6 Normalized Metrics
	•	revenue_per_guest = total_revenue / attendance
	•	capacity_utilization = attendance / capacity
	•	cost_per_guest = total_cost / attendance
	•	sponsor_roi = sponsor_value / total_revenue
	•	incident_rate = incidents / attendance × 1000
	•	nps = promoters - detractors
	•	conversion_rate = tickets_sold / visitors
9.7 Key Tables Reference
productions
Core entity: organization_id, title, format, status, dates, budgets, sensory_design (JSONB), xyz_foundation (JSONB), url_irl_journey (JSONB).
schedule_tasks
WHO (assignee, department, approver), WHAT (title, description), WHEN (dates, times, duration), WHERE (location, zone), WHY (purpose, impact), HOW (resources, budget), plus depends_on/blocks arrays.
task_contingencies
IF/THEN risk management: task_id, if_condition, then_action, escalation_contact_id, probability, impact, is_triggered.
shows
Performances: production_id, date, times, status, type, capacity, tickets_sold, attendance.
cues
Run of show: cue_number, scheduled_time, activity, department cues, talent, props, is_milestone.
incidents
Tracking: type, severity, status, description, persons_involved (JSONB), response_actions, medical/law_enforcement details.
9.8 Aggregation Views
	•	daily_metrics — Attendance and revenue by date
	•	production_summary — Shows, attendance, incidents, sponsors per production
	•	active_credentials — Currently valid credentials
	•	upcoming_tasks — Non-complete tasks with assignee info
9.9 Migration Phases
	•	Core: organizations, productions, venues, contacts
	•	Operational: credentials, schedules, shows, cues
	•	Compliance: contracts, permits, insurance
	•	Finance: sponsors, investors, expenses
	•	Reporting: incidents, daily_reports, wrap_reports
	•	Integrations: api_keys, webhooks, sync_logs
	•	Metrics: metrics table, audit_logs, views
9.10 Security Model
	•	RLS enabled on all tables
	•	Policies enforce organization_id via auth context
	•	API scopes: read/write:productions, read/write:operations, read/write:finance, admin
	•	Audit logs capture all access and modifications
	•	Sensitive fields encrypted at rest

